title: Change order form for HVAC (free PDF) | Jobchit
description: A free, printable HVAC change-order form. Record the equipment swap, tonnage and efficiency, refrigerant, duct, line set and thermostat changes, electrical work, the new total and both signatures. No account needed.
heading: Change order for HVAC
sub: For a bigger or more efficient unit, extra duct runs, a new thermostat or a damaged line set found mid-job. Write down the change and get both signatures before the work goes ahead.
tips:
  - Write the old and new equipment by make, model, size (tons or BTU) and efficiency (SEER2, HSPF2 or AFUE), so the price change is easy to follow.
  - Note the refrigerant type, and any charge added or recovered from the old system.
  - List duct runs, returns, registers or dampers added or moved, and any line set or condensate line replaced.
  - Record thermostat, zoning or electrical changes, such as a new disconnect, breaker or circuit.
  - Say whether the change affects the permit or inspection, and who registers the new equipment with the manufacturer.
  - Both sides sign and date it before the extra work starts. Give the customer a copy.
  - Some states have their own rules for change orders. Check with your state licensing board.
---
